I, too, want to commend you for the amount of work you've put into
this.

My biggest complaint is that my character doesn't seem to ever get
stronger.  I strongly advise against my character's strength being
based solely on the items he finds.  Also, the player's reward, in the
form of gold or whatever, seems to be left to chance and not to the
player's ability to kill or explore.   For comparison: Nethack's PC
has experience levels and weapon proficiencies, and killing certain
enemies is predictably rewarding (e.g. the dwarves in the mines drop
arms and armor).  Vaults are a regular occurrence.  In Gauntlet, the
player can accumulate powerups, health, and potions as a matter of
course, if he can survive long enough to acquire them.  Score is also
more a function of playtime than dungeon layout.

I'm not trying to criticize your game so much as point in the
direction I'd like to see it go.

Minor things:  I'd like the health display to be closer to the main
action.  At the moment it's hard to see when you're focusing on the
action.  I'd like to be able to open doors without taking my fingers
off the main action keys -- right now I much prefer to bash them down
than reach for 'o'.

Thanks for making this.  I hope you feel encouraged to continue.



